{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds","id":10982,"title":"Issues with Embeds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-14T19:04:21-08:00","id":10982,"title":"Issues with Embeds","content":"So don't know how receptive this is going to be but I currently have an issue with embeds. There are a few noticeable ones that I'll post later but my issue is both being free and reflexive. Maybe if they were all like just bruised where that has a limited number of uses in a scene but then there are others like turn blade which can be used five times a turn without a problem where things just get really silly. Then there's knockout punch which looks like it currently works on any being regardless of magical resistance. Which also brings me to the issue of why (Powerstat) doesn't apply to any of the powers that try to affect magical targets when it applies to a lot of powers across the board with other splats.<br /> <br /> Also, since embeds are exploiting the world naturally what happens when it's contesting something something blatantly magical. Like using Just Bruised against an astra or magical item that says it kills anything it touches or does an infinite number of successes? What happens when you try to erase the identity of someone capable of mystical forging one or unable to have theirs taken away? Do embeds just fail against these (Extremely niche and incredibly rare situations admittedly but I'd need to cross reference too many powers when I'm not feeling very well.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 11-14-2013, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T19:14:48-08:00","id":10990,"title":"","content":"I'd have my players roll for Compromise even for an embed in a situation like your just bruised situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T20:01:30-08:00","id":11014,"title":"","content":"In case of conflict, you'd use the power versus power rules as normal.<br /> <br /> As for embeds often being reflexive actions, no where in the rule book does it say you can do an infinite amount of reflexive actions a turn. <br /> <br /> The book says &quot;reflexive actions are best considered defensive or reactionary,&quot; and &quot;are resolved immediately after the instigating action or attack.&quot; <br /> <br /> So I'd say they can only do one active use of embeds a turn, as opposed to using defensive or reactionary embed use.<br /> <br /> But while that doesn't address turn blade, it's not like it's of infinite use. First of all, using it five times a turn is five times it can botch on the player, the attacker must be in line of sight and the demon has to know it's coming, and turn blade will never remove all damage by itself. Barring exceptional successes, the demon is going to take a minimum of five points of lethal damage, or enough bashing damage to knock them out. Being beaten down or knocked out is better than dead, sure but the demon is still in serious trouble there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T23:28:57-08:00","id":11087,"title":"","content":"Turn blade makes a weapon 0 if he twinks out for defense and/or has armor 5/4 he can pretty much negate it all, which isn't all that hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 11-15-2013, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T02:06:16-08:00","id":11124,"title":"","content":"although armorr can be ignored if you hit for example the unprotected head","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T05:25:11-08:00","id":11192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=11087#post11087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turn blade makes a weapon 0 if he twinks out for defense and/or has armor 5/4 he can pretty much negate it all, which isn't all that hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>So that demon is going to be hard as hell to hurt in a fight. Good job on the player. <br /> <br /> What's the issue?<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm sorry, I'm being obtuse. I know the issue, I just don't think it's an issue. Embeds, generally, do something very specific. They do what they do very, very well, but that just do that (some are more versatile than others, but they tend not to be AS reliable). I suspect that the words &quot;game balances&quot; are sneaking with ill-deserved gravity in the direction of this conversation, though. <br /> <br /> A demon that's good at combat is not better than anything else in any objective sense, because, as Storyteller, you should be able to use things that aren't combat to challenge characters and put some conflict in the story, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T05:32:42-08:00","id":11198,"title":"","content":"The armour itself is likely to be an issue - that's gotta be coming from Demonic Form (in which case, great, you're a combat monster when you're being open, but the more you do that the more angels show up to slot you) or you're stomping about in riot gear or a suit of full plate armour, in which case you're gonna have serious trouble getting into swanky parties or... well, anywhere except a medieval reenactment or the right kind of LARP, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T05:32:43-08:00","id":11199,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that a character walking aroun in 5/4 armor - which is to say, something tougher than either full plate or full riot gear - is going to be pretty bloody obvious, which is going to cause further problems","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T05:55:15-08:00","id":11209,"title":"","content":"I think someone (can't remember the name now) in another thread mentioned the fact that a lot of Embeds have &quot;sweeping&quot; (there word not mine) effects that are resisted by subtracted mechanics (e.g. - Stamina, Resolve, Composure, Defense).<br /> <br /> To my understanding it's the province of resistant mechanics (e.g. vs Resolve + Blood Potency) to oppose powers that have an everything or nothing affect. like a lot of Embeds. While powers that have increments of effect (e.g. each success = a point of damage) are opposed by subtracted mechanics. In addition, its rare that subtracted mechanics include a supernatural power stat in them, instead just using an attribute or derived stat. Meanwhile resistant mechanics almost always do involve a supernatural resistance trait. <br /> <br /> I was wondering, given this detail, if that was a purposeful design choice or not? Since previously in the other game lines the standard way a power is resisted was as I stated above. All or nothing affects are resisted and incremental affects are subtracted.<br /> <br /> Is the idea here that a lot of Embeds effect the Demon rather then the target directly. So as a result the supernatural nature of the opponent simply does not come into the equation? Alternatively, is it the idea that Embeds are functions of reality and therefore are supported by the the very structure of the NWoD, allowing them to sidestep or overpower a supernatural resistance trait?<br /> <br /> Basically, given the mechanical observations, I'm curious to know if there is an in-game reason why all or nothing powers are being given subtracted defenses rather then resistant ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T06:44:39-08:00","id":11230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=11199#post11199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that a character walking aroun in 5/4 armor - which is to say, something tougher than either full plate or full riot gear - is going to be pretty bloody obvious, which is going to cause further problems</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the only way you can specifically get that kind of rating, to my understanding, is by stacking the activated bonus from Aegis Protocol over Armored Plates, in which case\u2026 well, congratulations, you've deprived yourself of any other Processes until Primum 10 unless you take Terrible Form 4. (That reminds me, it's been observed that the name of the first dot of Terrible Form being the same as the name of a Process is a bit awkward; not sure if that's a thing that ought to/can be tweaked by this point.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:11:04-08:00","id":11251,"title":"","content":"I have issues with a number of powers but, if nothing else, I really hope the writers put a supernatural resistance roll on Knockout Punch. I'm not concerned about splat vs. splat balance because I know the games aren't meant to be balanced that way. It's just that, as written, it is kind of like Celerity in old Vampire: it has such a dramatic effect in combat that all combatants need to take it to be good in combat relative to people who do have it. Combat characters start to look samey as a result. Giving it the supernatural resistance roll would leave it as a great power, but not so great that it eclipses other options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/992-dionysos","name":"Dionysos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:15:53-08:00","id":11256,"title":"","content":"Also don't forget that the Storyteller is well within their rights to call for Compromise rolls if someone overuses an Embed. So, sure, use Turn Blade five times a turn for two or three turns straight. When the hunter angels come for you, that'll only last so long.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm just one of those Storytellers who loves to continue to hand rope to the PC's so that they might hang themselves. That could be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:25:31-08:00","id":11260,"title":"","content":"If you think a supernatural resistance roll for powers like Knockout Punch is appropriate, add one (my recommendation would be Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance). There's a section in Demon about why the Embeds work the way they do. You might not agree, but the choices aren't random. <br /> <br /> The other thing is, I'm not interested in white-room balance. I'm interested in making compelling stories and with what rules do to the narrative. I'm not seeing what the problem is. Is the problem that a demon could hypothetically be a raging, unstoppable combat monster? Is the problem that a demon could theoretically punch out an elder vampire or something? <br /> <br /> If the first...fine. The demon is a raging, unstoppable, combat monster. What does that mean for the story? Did the player communicate his/her desire to the Storyteller to be a RUCM, and will the Storyteller work that into the chronicle in a cool way? If not, why not? Is the player attempting to &quot;win&quot; the game by doing that? In that case, expectations need to be communicated more clearly. <br /> <br /> If the second, put that into context for me. Why is the demon punching a vampire? Why is that a problem for the players and the Storyteller? Is the player just doing that because s/he can, effectively trolling the group? If so, <i>that is not a game mechanics problem</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:32:09-08:00","id":11262,"title":"","content":"Matt I think you may be one of my favorite game designers ever, for that last line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:37:38-08:00","id":11267,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the response. My answer is that the problem is none of the above. The problem, like I said before, is that this one power has such an outsize impact on combat relative to other powers that all combatant characters will take and use it. If I have one combatant PC who takes it and two who do not, those latter two will see how amazing it is and buy it with experience soon afterward. Now combat is The Knockout Punch game. Combat characters start to feel the same in combat. It's like Celerity in old Vampire. It is so good relative to other options that combat becomes the Multiple Combat Actions game. It gives combat this kind of bland predictability that isn't very fun. But, obviously, it's your game so do what you like. I'll buy it either way (I'm a KS backer). I just want to try to help make the game as good as it can possibly be, because I love it in many ways as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/992-dionysos","name":"Dionysos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:38:50-08:00","id":11269,"title":"","content":"I think the problem for me would come from two points: 1) it <i>feels</i> wrong that an extremely potent being like an Elder Vampire should be trivially knocked out and 2) there's the weird cognitive dissonance that, should we get to the point of fighting the Elder Vampire, using the power would feel too easy for the Vampire's narrative role but <i>not</i> using it doesn't seem to make sense as a Thing My Character Would Do. This issue will show up with any form of attack that shortcuts past a big chunk of the combat system, since the narrative idea of &quot;this character is hard to defeat in combat&quot; is encoded into the mechanics.<br /> <br /> I agree completely about where the problem is when people are doing things to ruin the game, but if I have to make a decision where one choice simultaneously looks like it'll make the game less dramatic and fun but also is the obvious sensible choice for my character, that does nasty things to the way I enjoy games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:43:57-08:00","id":11273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dionysos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=11267#post11267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the response. My answer is that the problem is none of the above. The problem, like I said before, is that this one power has such an outsize impact on combat relative to other powers that all combatant characters will take and use it. If I have one combatant PC who takes it and two who do not, those latter two will see how amazing it is and buy it with experience soon afterward. Now combat is The Knockout Punch game. Combat characters start to feel the same in combat. It's like Celerity in old Vampire. It is so good relative to other options that combat becomes the Multiple Combat Actions game. It gives combat this kind of bland predictability that isn't very fun. But, obviously, it's your game so do what you like. I'll buy it either way (I'm a KS backer). I just want to try to help make the game as good as it can possibly be, because I love it in many ways as is.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're describing has not been my experience, running the game. I do take your point - certainly I try to avoid making powers that are so effective you're silly if you don't take them (Electroshock Recharge in Promethean was like that), but Knockout Punch is not, I think, in that category. Difference in players, perhaps? I don't know. Sure, it's an effective power, but so is Merciless Gunman, so is Hush, so is Ambush, etc. Depends how you want your demon to approach a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:45:50-08:00","id":11274,"title":"","content":"Actually, another issue is: Would the power work on a vampire at all, since head trauma doesn't matter as much (or in the same way) to vampires? <br /> <br /> The larger point this brings up is, we can't possible control for all of the hijinks your characters will get up to, which is why, hopefully, the metaphysical underpinnings of the powers are clear enough that, as Storyteller, you can adjudicate when something wonky happens. Even if that means going off-book, as it were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:31:48-08:00","id":11305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=11262#post11262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matt I think you may be one of my favorite game designers ever, for that last line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matt's one of more refreshing writers and developers out there quite often because he cuts through some of the more reverenced illusions about roleplaying games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T09:28:12-08:00","id":11342,"title":"","content":"Well, I base my design decisions on my experiences running/playing games in general, and on what my players (and players I've encountered at cons, etc., along the way) have found makes for good game. Basically it's a whole heap of anecdotal evidence, but I don't like making assumptions based on pure hypotheticals, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T09:30:59-08:00","id":11348,"title":"","content":"While it isn't explicitly written, I would assume any critter who normally can't be knocked out by damage would not be knocked out by the power. I believe right off hand (on vacation so I'm without books) that that is vampires, werewolves, prometheans, sin-eaters and mummies. So the bulk of critters would be immune.<br /> <br /> Likwise, since Just Bruised takes dice off successes, anything that is simply an insta-kill or provides unlimited successes or just doesn't work on a Health Levels of damage kind of effect wouldn't be subject to it, much like the old Exalted won't-keep-your-soul-from-getting-knocked-off effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T09:48:55-08:00","id":11369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=11273#post11273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, it's an effective power, but so is Merciless Gunman, so is Hush, so is Ambush, etc. Depends how you want your demon to approach a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hush really isn't a combat power so much as a utility and maybe tactical/strategy power. It's really cool, don't get me wrong, but as far as i can tell it doesn't give you any appreciable edge in the fight.<br /> <br /> Merciless Gunman is really really good during optional combat rules, but the 8-again really is just gonna buy you a turn or two. Likewise, Ambush buys you a turn.<br /> <br /> Knockout Punch is an I-Win-Button. You can get hit with Ambush or Merciless Gunman or Hush and it will suck, but it's recoverable. Knockout Punch means game over, no chance.<br /> <br /> Lovely game by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T10:01:03-08:00","id":11381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=11260#post11260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think a supernatural resistance roll for powers like Knockout Punch is appropriate, add one (my recommendation would be Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance). There's a section in Demon about why the Embeds work the way they do. You might not agree, but the choices aren't random.<br /> <br /> The other thing is, I'm not interested in white-room balance. I'm interested in making compelling stories and with what rules do to the narrative. I'm not seeing what the problem is. Is the problem that a demon could hypothetically be a raging, unstoppable combat monster? Is the problem that a demon could theoretically punch out an elder vampire or something?<br /> <br /> If the first...fine. The demon is a raging, unstoppable, combat monster. What does that mean for the story? Did the player communicate his/her desire to the Storyteller to be a RUCM, and will the Storyteller work that into the chronicle in a cool way? If not, why not? Is the player attempting to &quot;win&quot; the game by doing that? In that case, expectations need to be communicated more clearly.<br /> <br /> If the second, put that into context for me. Why is the demon punching a vampire? Why is that a problem for the players and the Storyteller? Is the player just doing that because s/he can, effectively trolling the group? If so, <i>that is not a game mechanics problem</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue with specific embeds is that it makes a fight a one-sided battle. Makes an aspect of the game either boring or pointless. At least just bruised has a limited window. Turn blade with 8 dice only fails if the characters has pretty bad luck.<br /> <br /> My question about Knockout punch is how embeds work on beings INCAPABLE of being effected by it. It says they are exploits of reality that means logically that the fundamental nature of embeds are Mundane and can't override Magical aspects of reality. I'm asking if this assumption is true or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T10:31:32-08:00","id":11411,"title":"","content":"Knockout Punch isn't that singularly amazing. There's a lot of ways for demons to make one hit fight-ending for the target - Blade Hand can do 5L+ in a single hit, or Cavernous Maw can do 3A+ targetted to a limb. In the right contexts - ambush, nonlethally dropping mooks (make it an Interlock with Merciless Gunman for kung fu fun), bumrushing - KP's really useful.<br /> <br /> It is not the best combat power, not least because if it doesn't land, nothing happens. It's a straight pool of Dexterity+Brawl with defense subtracted, which means you have only one skill and one attribute up against GMC defense levels. There's not a lot you can do to inflate your pool, especially compared to using a light weapon, or a firearm (or rivet arm). And every time you miss is a -1 to later attempts in the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","user":"Nicias","date":". 11-15-2013, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T11:08:00-08:00","id":11426,"title":"","content":"Leaving aside combat-specific things, here are my Embed problems:<br /> <br /> 1. Why does Manipulation get everything? There are 47 Manipulation + powers, 5 Dexterity + powers, and 25 Wits + powers. A lot of them make sense to be Manipulation-based because they're things involving screwing with language nad heads. But then you get Manipulation subbing for anything from resolving binary events (Left or Right?), to pure luck (Lucky Break), to providing raw materials ex nihilo (Raw Materials), or ruining aim (Check Backdrop). I get that Manipulation doesn't contribute to combat like Wits does, or double-up on combat helping like Dexterity does, but it just feels like a crappy limitation in character-design-space when your options for subtle, insidious power use are &quot;be good at lying, also&quot; or else you throw out a little under 2/3 of your options.<br /> <br /> 2. Why's there an overlap on some things, and why's Manipulation still get the best of it in that context? I'm looking specifically at Raw Materials, Sabotage, and Shatter (pp 186-7). Just three powers in a row, doing similar things, with wildly varying efficacy.<br /> <br /> Raw Materials: Manipulation. Breaks the target object no matter what, brings a replacement depending on success, might blow Cover on a dramatic failure.<br /> Sabotage: Dexterity. Shuts down the object until someone gets a few successes to repair it, harder to fix with exceptional successes, forces a compromise check on dramatic failure.<br /> Shatter: Wits. Breaks an object of Size (Yours or lower), risks blowing Cover if the object was above a Durability threshold, can have a delayed effect on exceptional success, hurts you on a dramatic failure.<br /> <br /> Why are there three of these, and why is the Manipulation one straight-up the best at actually doing the &quot;break a thing&quot; thing? It's not even the main effect of the power, but it's guaranteed with the added bonus of getting a replacement later (which would be handy if you're banking on something like surrendering yourself into custody or somesuch). The Dex one is the most subtle of them (and the only one that's temporary, really), unless you can get exceptional successes on the Wits one. And the Wits one is the only one to come with so many limitations---can't be above size X, risks blowing cover above Durability Y, straight up damages you on a dramatic failure.<br /> <br /> Now, IN A PERFECT WORLD, it would be super-cool if this kind of thing was part of a framework for effectively making almost any Embed &quot;castable&quot; via one of the three Finesse attributes (almost something akin to Geist keys being applied to Manifestations), but in practice it's just...here, which of these three ways of breaking stuff do you want: the one that might hurt you, the one that's only temporary, or the one that gives you an added bonus later? <br /> <br /> In general though, Demon's a really cool game idea, the space it occupies for espionage-but-with-powers, angelic/demonic-without-strictly-Judeo-Christian, Matrix-without-being-owoddy-90s is amazing. And a ton of the Embed/Exploit ideas themselves are amazing (pun power alone has my entire group yelling at each other and pointing fingers over who has to run a campaign for the rest of us to play in). I just wish the Embeds were anywhere near as stat-balanced for choices as the Exploits are (they're a much closer 11/12/17 split between key attributes, at least).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/265-cbn","name":"CBN","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T12:15:13-08:00","id":11466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=11260#post11260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think a supernatural resistance roll for powers like Knockout Punch is appropriate, add one (my recommendation would be Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance). There's a section in Demon about why the Embeds work the way they do. You might not agree, but the choices aren't random.<br /> <br /> The other thing is, I'm not interested in white-room balance. I'm interested in making compelling stories and with what rules do to the narrative. I'm not seeing what the problem is. Is the problem that a demon could hypothetically be a raging, unstoppable combat monster? Is the problem that a demon could theoretically punch out an elder vampire or something?<br /> <br /> If the first...fine. The demon is a raging, unstoppable, combat monster. What does that mean for the story? Did the player communicate his/her desire to the Storyteller to be a RUCM, and will the Storyteller work that into the chronicle in a cool way? If not, why not? Is the player attempting to &quot;win&quot; the game by doing that? In that case, expectations need to be communicated more clearly.<br /> <br /> If the second, put that into context for me. Why is the demon punching a vampire? Why is that a problem for the players and the Storyteller? Is the player just doing that because s/he can, effectively trolling the group? If so, <i>that is not a game mechanics problem</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why we get along so well. It is also full of all of the win.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T12:19:47-08:00","id":11472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=11369#post11369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hush really isn't a combat power so much as a utility and maybe tactical/strategy power. It's really cool, don't get me wrong, but as far as i can tell it doesn't give you any appreciable edge in the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I let one of my players use Hush, Strike First, and Knockout Punch pretty much all together. There was a very small amount of prep time, but basically I let him break all the rules because the image of him swiftly and silently knocking a dude out while he was taking a piss (don't ask; we had one session where everything pretty much went to hell - no pun intended) was amusing and cool. And it fit the story at the time, so I let it slide.<br /> <br /> The more I've been erring on the side of &quot;man, that'll be cool if you can do that,&quot; the more fun we've been having in our gaming sessions, regardless of system. That's not for everybody, but we've been having a blast.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T12:54:01-08:00","id":11509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=11411#post11411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knockout Punch isn't that singularly amazing. There's a lot of ways for demons to make one hit fight-ending for the target - Blade Hand can do 5L+ in a single hit, or Cavernous Maw can do 3A+ targetted to a limb. In the right contexts - ambush, nonlethally dropping mooks (make it an Interlock with Merciless Gunman for kung fu fun), bumrushing - KP's really useful.<br /> <br /> It is not the best combat power, not least because if it doesn't land, nothing happens. It's a straight pool of Dexterity+Brawl with defense subtracted, which means you have only one skill and one attribute up against GMC defense levels. There's not a lot you can do to inflate your pool, especially compared to using a light weapon, or a firearm (or rivet arm). And every time you miss is a -1 to later attempts in the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is where you are wrong. It is the best combat power because if it hits the fight is over. The target can't do anything and you can just finish him off. If it lands with one success or twenty doesn't matter what the target is incapacitated and now you can finish him off at your leisure or keep him in a coma indefinitely. I'm talking about Spirit 4 beings being put down in one attack when it would otherwise be near impossible to touch them otherwise. Blade Hand and Carenous maw against a combat twinked angel means they get about 1 or two damage max per turn, sssuming that the demon can even touch him in the first place. This just needs one success to succeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T13:22:36-08:00","id":11528,"title":"","content":"What kind of fourth rank angel can resist 5L+ but goes down in one hit without waking up when he's attacked again? I read the end of that writeup as &quot;killing someone vulnerable from KP always calls for a compromise roll,&quot; not &quot;you can magically kill anyone while they're knocked out.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T13:34:12-08:00","id":11533,"title":"","content":"Well, to be fair, it does say &quot;You can kill anyone you've KO'd with this power&quot;, but it also says &quot;Be prepared for losing a dot of Cover, maybe gaining a Beat from it if you're particularly unlucky, because you're murdering someone with a -3 and possibly more on your Cover roll depending on other modifiers&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T15:04:54-08:00","id":11610,"title":"","content":"I'm making one last contribution to the &quot;should Knockout Punch be toned down?&quot; discussion. Because I have a strict personal limit of three posts in any internet argument about elfgames. Also, I really want to avoid the impression of being antagonistic, because that is really not my goal here.<br /> <br /> First, the fact that you are discouraged from killing the people you knocked out doesn't make it much less of an &quot;I Win Button&quot;. You could walk past the unconscious Big Bad and disrupt his nefarious plot. You could just run away and escape from the unconscious destroyer angel who had tracked you down. Hell, if this person really needs to die, you could take his indefinitely unconscious body somewhere else, restrain him and kill him after he wakes up sometime later. On the rare occasions that none of these will do, you could take the hit to cover. It is manageable if only done occasionally.<br /> <br /> @Blackhatmatt: You suggested that the issue might be that you've played with one kind of player group and I with another. That is totally, absolutely the case here. My group includes three players who usually try to build strong combat characters and look for optimal ways to do that. The other three are agnostic about this, they could be good in combat or not. They don't much care. If someone else in the group is way better at combat than they are, they aren't too bothered. I'm guessing most of your players are like these latter three of mine. Cool.<br /> <br /> Your kind of group isn't unusual in my experience, <i>but neither is mine</i>. So probably the best thing to do would be to find a solution that both kinds of groups would be happy with.<br /> <br /> Let's assume that Knockout Punch stays the way it is. Your group is obviously cool with that. In mine, though, I'm going to need to houserule it (and so will the many other groups that have player distributions like mine). I've outlined the reasons above: KP is such a great combat power relative to the others that all three of my combatant types are going to gravitate toward it, whether at first or after seeing it in action. Combat encounters will be Knockout Punch marathons. I'll need to add the resistance roll to put it on the same level as other options.<br /> <br /> But what happens if KP gets a contested supernaturat resistance trait roll added to it before the game goes to press? Well, my group can play without any houserules required, and so can the other groups that are similar to mine. KP remains a great power, but the resistance roll means that it is not quite so reliable against supernatural antagonists. It has benefits and drawbacks. Maybe a given player wants that one, maybe she wants other stuff instead. Diverse character powers are the result. Awesome.<br /> <br /> And your group and groups like them? They are cool with this too! They aren't too bothered about optimal combat stuff, so whether or not KP allows for supernatural resistance rolls doesn't impact them too much either way. They'll take it or not, depending on whether it fits the fiction of the character concept that they have decided upon. Diverse character powers are the result. Awesome.<br /> <br /> So, this being the case, doesn't it make sense to add the supernatural resistance roll to KP? It is the solution that everyone can be happy with.<br /> <br /> Thanks for engaging with the fans over this stuff. We just like your games and want to help out to smooth rough edges when possible. And since Demon hasn't gone to print yet, we feel like this is the perfect time to try to get this sort of thing addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/992-dionysos","user":"Dionysos","date":". 11-15-2013, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/992-dionysos","name":"Dionysos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T15:15:20-08:00","id":11618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=11528#post11528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of fourth rank angel can resist 5L+ but goes down in one hit without waking up when he's attacked again? I read the end of that writeup as &quot;killing someone vulnerable from KP always calls for a compromise roll,&quot; not &quot;you can magically kill anyone while they're knocked out.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Influences and numina go away after the scene ends (IE knocked out and combat is over) unless he permanently has 5 armor as an innate feature. Compromise rolls don't matter when the person you've killed is dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T16:45:11-08:00","id":11673,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that they do, because should you fail, your cover gets that much shakier. It's not just the one person who compromised you. Your entire cover is now a little shakier. You're one step closer to being Burned and having to look for a new Cover. And living Burned... well, as Michael Westen could tell you, living after you've been Burned is no picnic. And that goes double for a Demon. At least double.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T17:31:45-08:00","id":11721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=11618#post11618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Influences and numina go away after the scene ends (IE knocked out and combat is over) unless he permanently has 5 armor as an innate feature. Compromise rolls don't matter when the person you've killed is dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very much A TAKE on that situation. I don't however, believe it to be the default take of Demon (if such a thing exists). <br /> <br /> Firstly, as the ST its entirely up to you if the scene is &quot;over&quot; once combat is over. Sometimes that might be thematically appropriate, other times, not so much. <br /> <br /> Secondly, the fact that you loose cover is a much bigger deal then killing one angel. There are always more angels. You managed to take down a single hunter-killer, congratulations. With your cover reduced the chances that you'll have to face more of them later goes up. Knock Out Punch or no, you can't survive 5 hunter-killer rank 3+ angels descending on your position when you next screw up. <br /> <br /> Thirdly, to my knowledge Angel's don't fall unconscious. So Knock Out Punch does not likely work on them. <br /> <br /> In general I don't think every power needs to quantify every aspect of itself, people can use &quot;common sense&quot; and a general idea of the games thematics to guide them a lot of the time. If something has no unconscious state e.g. Vampires, Geists, Mummy's, Prometheans, Ghosts, Gentry, Spirits, Angels and Demons in their True Form, then it cannot be put in such a state by a power designed to knock-out things out. Things that can be knocked out e.g. Humans, Werewolves, Changelings, Mages can be. Template features always override powers unless otherwise directly stated, for example, a power that negates magical regeneration specifically e.g. Kiss of Apep from Mummy, would negate a Werewolf's healing factor. <br /> <br /> Does this make Demons &quot;better&quot; against some other supernaturals compared with others. Yeah, but none of these games have ever been cross-balanced. Nor should they be, as it would likely hurt the feel and thematic of each. <br /> <br /> Sorry if any of that came off as overly confrontational. Just that when I was reading the embed section of the book I found the preface to it that talks about making powers work with game tone and thematics pretty much cleared up any vagaries for me. With Matt talking about the stuff on here only backing up that interpretation. So I guess I just got a little frustrated that other people seem to not get this idea of &quot;common sense&quot; and narrative function with powers. I know its not everyones cup of tea and I should be more understanding of it, but after it's an argument I see repeated for three pages I felt the need to highlight the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T18:43:08-08:00","id":11766,"title":"","content":"I'ma just put this here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...lvXIq9fI/edit#</a><br /> <br /> That should resolve any crossover concerns or balance issues, for those who have them. Changes are in Blue, flat out removals in red.<br /> <br /> (Hopefully this isn't overstepping, what with the rules being on the KS page. But if it is I'll take this down)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-15-2013, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T20:31:52-08:00","id":11833,"title":"","content":"End of the fight isn't really the end of the scene, although it's close. The scene ends when the characters transition to a new location. That's what a scene is at it's core. If you get into a shootout at a diner and the cops come, the scene ends when the characters decide to cheese it and run to a new location. Aftermath of a fight is just as much part of the same scene unless there is some sort of greater transition. (Notably that transition can be emotional or symbolic rather than physical, so while the characters are in the same physical location the nature of that location has changed enough that it's effectively a new scene. My point still stands though.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T00:16:05-08:00","id":11938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=11833#post11833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">End of the fight isn't really the end of the scene, although it's close. The scene ends when the characters transition to a new location. That's what a scene is at it's core. If you get into a shootout at a diner and the cops come, the scene ends when the characters decide to cheese it and run to a new location. Aftermath of a fight is just as much part of the same scene unless there is some sort of greater transition. (Notably that transition can be emotional or symbolic rather than physical, so while the characters are in the same physical location the nature of that location has changed enough that it's effectively a new scene. My point still stands though.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You can make it last indefinitely or at least long enough to kill him defenselessly so it wouldn't matter. He could also just have someone else kill him for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T00:50:11-08:00","id":11943,"title":"","content":"<b>@Matt:</b> In many ways you are correct. If the players wish to play Demon-as-unstoppable-monster and the ST is okay with running that type of game, then they should be able to. More importantly, Demon: the Descent is the type of game where that should be possible. Likewise, white-room balance is significantly less important that actual story balance. However, you ask a very insightful question I'd like to turn around. If I am playing the aforementioned rampaging Demon, what effect does taking Knockout Punch have on the story we are telling? How does that effect presented in that way add to the theme of the rampaging demon, or make playing it out more interesting for everyone at the table?<br /> <br /> As a ST, it is my job both to provide the players with challenges that are outside their expertise or require lateral thought. It is also my job to give the players opportunities to show off and present challenges that are inside my purview. If I have a player who is a rampaging monster Demon, it is important to supply mooks who are eaten and great monsters that are worthy challenges to their skills. What tools do I have to challenge a combat-specced Demon in an interesting way with the material presented? How can I do so without making the rest of the group feel useless.<br /> <br /> In the case of Demon, this is of a particular concern. Part of Demon-as-presented is this idea that you are being actively hunted by a tremendous physical threat--Angels. A Demon's ability to mitigate that threat has a rather direct impact on the stories told.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T01:59:43-08:00","id":11969,"title":"","content":"To address Epimetheus's point about knocked out enemies -<br /> <br /> I don't remember reading anywhere that Angel's get knocked out in general. Hell, even in their cover they don't eat or sleep unless they choose to. So I have no reason to believe they react to blunt force trauma the same way Humans do. Certainly I doubt that's the case in their true forms. So like with Vampires, Mummy's etc, I doubt knock-out punch will work on them in the first place.<br /> <br /> Just be absolutely clear to your players when you start the game that Knock Out Punch does not work on things that can't be knocked out. Once that principle is in place you should avoid any later strife with the players over the powers usage. As it basically means is useful only against certain targets. In a pure Demon game that's Humans, Stigmatics, some Cryptids and Demons in Cover which you get the drop on (once again I am pretty sure Demon's can't fall unconscious in their true forms). .<br /> <br /> This also kinda deals with one of SoulGambits issues as well. As knock-out punch is no longer useful against Angels then it does nothing to hurt the idea that they are a very dangerous physical threat if confronted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T06:07:18-08:00","id":13964,"title":"","content":"So, I have no idea if this little anecdote will help or hurt, but I'm gonna do it anyway.<br /> <br /> When I was running the SAS, the characters wound up talking to Simon Flannery (the main antagonist). They knew he was a demon, and so they knew they couldn't trust anything he said, because you can't ever tell if a demon is lying, but they weren't sure exactly what he was up to and how much they should get involved. And one of the characters used Freudian Slip on him. <br /> <br /> Pause time for a moment, and gaze into the Stygian abyss of my brain as I'm Storytelling. <br /> <br /> <i>Should this power work...from a story perspective?</i> Yes, absolutely. The narrative flow of the scene was leading to a confrontation. The pacing of the game was leading to this being the last or next-to-last session (turned out to be the next-to-last). The characters already suspected Simon was shady, they just needed a little more information. <br /> <br /> <i>Should this power work...from a mechanics perspective?</i> Not really. Freudian Slip specifically says it doesn't work on demons (though in fairness, I think I added that note after I ran this game). You can't <i>make</i> a demon do anything honestly, even a knee-jerk reaction. <br /> <br /> So why did I let it work? (Well, because it was a playtest, but if I were running the game now, I'd do the same thing.)<br /> <br /> For one thing, because the player was excited about it. If I said 'no,' I'd have been stepping on her toes. That's bad form as an ST.<br /> For another, because it was the best thing for the story. <br /> And for yet another, because <i>in this context</i>, it made sense. Simon is a low-Cover demon and a dedicated Integrator. He was on edge anyway, and there was so much magic flying around at that particular point in the game that it wasn't hard to imagine that his control might be a little wonky. <i>And</i>, Simon is a self-sabotaging sort of demon anyway. <br /> <br /> My point in all of this is not (just) to say &quot;fiddle with the rules to serve the story;&quot; I think we can take that as read. My point is that it's not unreasonable for the Storyteller to examine a situation in context and make decisions on how a power works within that context. It's not unreasonable for a player to say, &quot;Hey, I think this should work this way&quot; and for the Storyteller to say, &quot;sure, that's cool, but it normally doesn't work that way, so don't get used to this.&quot; It's not unreasonable for a Storyteller to say, &quot;this power doesn't specifically <i>say</i> it works/doesn't work on vampires, but knowing what I do about vampire physiology as defined in <b>The Blood</b>, I think it should/shouldn't.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T06:08:02-08:00","id":13965,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I don't think I'd let Knockout Punch work on an angel. But it would depend on the angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T03:02:13-08:00","id":15277,"title":"","content":"If the game rules are there for breaking / ignoring why have them at all? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T03:10:58-08:00","id":15278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=15277#post15277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the game rules are there for breaking / ignoring why have them at all? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Peraphs as guide ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T04:17:43-08:00","id":15293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=13964#post13964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have no idea if this little anecdote will help or hurt, but I'm gonna do it anyway.<br /> <br /> When I was running the SAS, the characters wound up talking to Simon Flannery (the main antagonist). They knew he was a demon, and so they knew they couldn't trust anything he said, because you can't ever tell if a demon is lying, but they weren't sure exactly what he was up to and how much they should get involved. And one of the characters used Freudian Slip on him.<br /> <br /> Pause time for a moment, and gaze into the Stygian abyss of my brain as I'm Storytelling.<br /> <br /> <i>Should this power work...from a story perspective?</i> Yes, absolutely. The narrative flow of the scene was leading to a confrontation. The pacing of the game was leading to this being the last or next-to-last session (turned out to be the next-to-last). The characters already suspected Simon was shady, they just needed a little more information.<br /> <br /> <i>Should this power work...from a mechanics perspective?</i> Not really. Freudian Slip specifically says it doesn't work on demons (though in fairness, I think I added that note after I ran this game). You can't <i>make</i> a demon do anything honestly, even a knee-jerk reaction.<br /> <br /> So why did I let it work? (Well, because it was a playtest, but if I were running the game now, I'd do the same thing.)<br /> <br /> For one thing, because the player was excited about it. If I said 'no,' I'd have been stepping on her toes. That's bad form as an ST.<br /> For another, because it was the best thing for the story.<br /> And for yet another, because <i>in this context</i>, it made sense. Simon is a low-Cover demon and a dedicated Integrator. He was on edge anyway, and there was so much magic flying around at that particular point in the game that it wasn't hard to imagine that his control might be a little wonky. <i>And</i>, Simon is a self-sabotaging sort of demon anyway.<br /> <br /> My point in all of this is not (just) to say &quot;fiddle with the rules to serve the story;&quot; I think we can take that as read. My point is that it's not unreasonable for the Storyteller to examine a situation in context and make decisions on how a power works within that context. It's not unreasonable for a player to say, &quot;Hey, I think this should work this way&quot; and for the Storyteller to say, &quot;sure, that's cool, but it normally doesn't work that way, so don't get used to this.&quot; It's not unreasonable for a Storyteller to say, &quot;this power doesn't specifically <i>say</i> it works/doesn't work on vampires, but knowing what I do about vampire physiology as defined in <b>The Blood</b>, I think it should/shouldn't.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be nice to have a clearer rules system. Rather than just leaving it to the ST because it just bogs down the game if you have to look at a power and then on the spot have to deal with a player who goes, &quot;I doesn't say it can't.&quot; And then having a debate with an st for at least half an hour. I don't need exacting yes and no rules but there are a number of powers that just ruin the game when used wholesale and keeping them vague just makes them more of a headache to have in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 11-21-2013, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T04:50:24-08:00","id":15309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=15293#post15293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be nice to have a clearer rules system. Rather than just leaving it to the ST because it just bogs down the game if you have to look at a power and then on the spot have to deal with a player who goes, &quot;I doesn't say it can't.&quot; And then having a debate with an st for at least half an hour. I don't need exacting yes and no rules but there are a number of powers that just ruin the game when used wholesale and keeping them vague just makes them more of a headache to have in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see your point here. I find a good way around this issue is to make it clear to your players what you want from the game right at the start. Demon encourages the players to make their PC's together with some ST input. Just make it perfectly clear during character gen that Knock-Out punch only works on normal humans, if that's what you want. If you want it to work on Stigmatic's and Cryptids as well then say so. If you want it to work on anything that is &quot;alive&quot; then say so. If you want to rule that it can knock Vampires into temporary Torpor then say so. <br /> <br /> Its a 30 second announcement of your intent as storyteller to treat that embed in a certain way to reinforce whatever themes you are going for in your Demon game. Not a half-an-hour argument when it comes up in play and the player is working under one assumption and your working under another. <br /> <br /> Also as ST, I find having a firmer hand in general works. If you have players pulling the &quot;It doesn't say I can't&quot; argument certail that crap. Its frankly bad roleplay etiquette as far as I am concerned, it reeks of looking for exploits in a game system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T07:45:35-08:00","id":16105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=15277#post15277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the game rules are there for breaking / ignoring why have them at all? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Really? <br /> <br /> OK, sure. The rules aren't there for breaking/ignoring. They're there to facilitate awesome stories about Fallen biomechanical angels. If at any point the rules aren't doing that, it's worth trying to figure out why. <br /> <br /> Let's go back to my example with Freudian Slip. Let's say that Amy (the demon who used that power on Simon) had done so one session earlier, on Comrade West, as they were talking about the Demon's Republic of Seattle in Priscilla's apartment (you want context, read the SAS, I'm on the clock, here). If she had, it wouldn't have worked. <br /> <br /> Why? Because West, though he may be low-Cover, depending on the day, is a very much in-control-of-himself demon. The scene wasn't set in a time-splinter, nor was there an inordinate amount of magic flying around. More to the point, it wouldn't have remotely served the story for the power to work in a non-standard way.<br /> <br /> The answer is, you have the rules to provide <i>context</i>, but, likewise, the rules only work <i>in context</i>. It's why I don't like ruling on hypotheticals, and my answer is usually &quot;I don't know, it would depend on what you want to do with your game.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T10:16:47-08:00","id":16158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dionysos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=11610#post11610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm making one last contribution to the &quot;should Knockout Punch be toned down?&quot; discussion. Because I have a strict personal limit of three posts in any internet argument about elfgames. Also, I really want to avoid the impression of being antagonistic, because that is really not my goal here.<br /> <br /> First, the fact that you are discouraged from killing the people you knocked out doesn't make it much less of an &quot;I Win Button&quot;. You could walk past the unconscious Big Bad and disrupt his nefarious plot. You could just run away and escape from the unconscious destroyer angel who had tracked you down. Hell, if this person really needs to die, you could take his indefinitely unconscious body somewhere else, restrain him and kill him after he wakes up sometime later. On the rare occasions that none of these will do, you could take the hit to cover. It is manageable if only done occasionally.<br /> <br /> @Blackhatmatt: You suggested that the issue might be that you've played with one kind of player group and I with another. That is totally, absolutely the case here. My group includes three players who usually try to build strong combat characters and look for optimal ways to do that. The other three are agnostic about this, they could be good in combat or not. They don't much care. If someone else in the group is way better at combat than they are, they aren't too bothered. I'm guessing most of your players are like these latter three of mine. Cool.<br /> <br /> Your kind of group isn't unusual in my experience, <i>but neither is mine</i>. So probably the best thing to do would be to find a solution that both kinds of groups would be happy with.<br /> <br /> Let's assume that Knockout Punch stays the way it is. Your group is obviously cool with that. In mine, though, I'm going to need to houserule it (and so will the many other groups that have player distributions like mine). I've outlined the reasons above: KP is such a great combat power relative to the others that all three of my combatant types are going to gravitate toward it, whether at first or after seeing it in action. Combat encounters will be Knockout Punch marathons. I'll need to add the resistance roll to put it on the same level as other options.<br /> <br /> But what happens if KP gets a contested supernaturat resistance trait roll added to it before the game goes to press? Well, my group can play without any houserules required, and so can the other groups that are similar to mine. KP remains a great power, but the resistance roll means that it is not quite so reliable against supernatural antagonists. It has benefits and drawbacks. Maybe a given player wants that one, maybe she wants other stuff instead. Diverse character powers are the result. Awesome.<br /> <br /> And your group and groups like them? They are cool with this too! They aren't too bothered about optimal combat stuff, so whether or not KP allows for supernatural resistance rolls doesn't impact them too much either way. They'll take it or not, depending on whether it fits the fiction of the character concept that they have decided upon. Diverse character powers are the result. Awesome.<br /> <br /> So, this being the case, doesn't it make sense to add the supernatural resistance roll to KP? It is the solution that everyone can be happy with.<br /> <br /> Thanks for engaging with the fans over this stuff. We just like your games and want to help out to smooth rough edges when possible. And since Demon hasn't gone to print yet, we feel like this is the perfect time to try to get this sort of thing addressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just house-rule it and be done with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T10:42:12-08:00","id":16175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=15277#post15277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the game rules are there for breaking / ignoring why have them at all? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Rules exist for those who are not yet comfortable breaking them. New storytellers and beginner players who love the ideas, but don't yet have a grasp for the system. As well as experienced roleplayers who simply don't have a head for numbers. They exist to help reign in power gamers and overzealous Storytellers, and keep everyone on roughly the same level (theme-wise, not D&amp;D power level). I can't count the number of times having hard rules helped me reign in and refine a character (both PCs and NPCs) who was getting out of hand, and resulted in a better character overall.<br /> <br /> Put simply, every system is someone's first system, and rules are there to help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T11:29:45-08:00","id":16200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=16105#post16105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Really? OK, sure. The rules aren't there for breaking/ignoring. They're there to facilitate awesome stories about Fallen biomechanical angels. If at any point the rules aren't doing that, it's worth trying to figure out why. Let's go back to my example with Freudian Slip. Let's say that Amy (the demon who used that power on Simon) had done so one session earlier, on Comrade West, as they were talking about the Demon's Republic of Seattle in Priscilla's apartment (you want context, read the SAS, I'm on the clock, here). If she had, it wouldn't have worked. Why? Because West, though he may be low-Cover, depending on the day, is a very much in-control-of-himself demon. The scene wasn't set in a time-splinter, nor was there an inordinate amount of magic flying around. More to the point, it wouldn't have remotely served the story for the power to work in a non-standard way. The answer is, you have the rules to provide <i>context</i>, but, likewise, the rules only work <i>in context</i>. It's why I don't like ruling on hypotheticals, and my answer is usually &quot;I don't know, it would depend on what you want to do with your game.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Many, many players are not ok with the rules working a certain way some of the time, and a different way other times. Now, I happen to agree with you that the rules are nice guidelines that should facilitate roleplay when they improve the story, and get out of the way when they don't. But I have encountered enough people who simply cannot enjoy a game unless the rules are ironclad, objective facts of the game reality - almost more like a video game's physics engine than tools for telling stories. I, as someone comfortable bending or breaking rules, am perfectly happy having thoroughly defined, physics like rules, because I know I can change them if I need to and my group will understand. But someone who needs those rules-as-physical-laws will simply not have fun with soft, malleable rules. Is it not then better to have rules that work for both parties than rules that only work for those of us who are just going to ignore them anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T13:39:38-08:00","id":16260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=16200#post16200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Many, many players are not ok with the rules working a certain way some of the time, and a different way other times. Now, I happen to agree with you that the rules are nice guidelines that should facilitate roleplay when they improve the story, and get out of the way when they don't. But I have encountered enough people who simply cannot enjoy a game unless the rules are ironclad, objective facts of the game reality - almost more like a video game's physics engine than tools for telling stories. I, as someone comfortable bending or breaking rules, am perfectly happy having thoroughly defined, physics like rules, because I know I can change them if I need to and my group will understand. But someone who needs those rules-as-physical-laws will simply not have fun with soft, malleable rules. Is it not then better to have rules that work for both parties than rules that only work for those of us who are just going to ignore them anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't a roleplaying game where this is a thing. No system, no matter how complex, can assume every eventuality. World of Darkness products have never <i>tried</i> to be perfect engines of interaction with the world. The games that <i>have </i>tried? Hilarious.<br /> <br /> Even the most hard core simulationist is going to have to make choices arbitrarily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T13:54:39-08:00","id":16270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrophelean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=16260#post16260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There isn't a roleplaying game where this is a thing. No system, no matter how complex, can assume every eventuality. World of Darkness products have never <i>tried</i> to be perfect engines of interaction with the world. The games that <i>have </i>tried? Hilarious. Even the most hard core simulationist is going to have to make choices arbitrarily.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree, I think simulationism is a bizarre playstyle, I've never understood it. But I can still have a fun time playing more simulationist-oriented games because I bend the rules where I need to. But I also have friends who I've never been able to get into WoD because it's too narrativist for them to enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T15:13:45-08:00","id":16304,"title":"","content":"Asking for clarification and stricter limits on a power that has the potential to outshine all other features a combatant could have in many situations is not going to turn the game into FATAL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:41:59-08:00","id":16397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=16304#post16304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asking for clarification and stricter limits on a power that has the potential to outshine all other features a combatant could have in many situations is not going to turn the game into FATAL.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Key word there is &quot;Potential&quot;. As has been mentioned multiple times in this thread, its a power that requires an ST to basically decide the exact remit of how it works when he/she decides to run Demon. If you want a game where Knock Out Punch is the undisputed combat power, then you let it work on anything and everything. If not then you simply tell your players at character gen what you do plan on having Knock Out Punch work on e.g. all living creatures but not undead, only humans with no supernatural element, only humans without a major template. <br /> <br /> Really, its a pretty simple answer and I from what Matt has been saying, he's not doing to be editing the power before the PDF comes out. So if you want a &quot;fix&quot; for the power your own judgement as an ST is going to be the only one you are going to get likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T20:44:52-08:00","id":16444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=16397#post16397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Key word there is &quot;Potential&quot;. As has been mentioned multiple times in this thread, its a power that requires an ST to basically decide the exact remit of how it works when he/she decides to run Demon. If you want a game where Knock Out Punch is the undisputed combat power, then you let it work on anything and everything. If not then you simply tell your players at character gen what you do plan on having Knock Out Punch work on e.g. all living creatures but not undead, only humans with no supernatural element, only humans without a major template.<br /> <br /> Really, its a pretty simple answer and I from what Matt has been saying, he's not doing to be editing the power before the PDF comes out. So if you want a &quot;fix&quot; for the power your own judgement as an ST is going to be the only one you are going to get likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knock Out Punch was the one that I brought up off the top of my head but there are a number of powers that just bring up number of issues. For the most part, like Pendragon said this isn't going to be an issue with experienced ST's they'll look at a power and go, &quot;Yeah that doesn't work in this situation because that would be dumb.&quot; someone starting out is going to look at something like killing kittens with shift consequences to kill angels and go, &quot;A-Alright that works.&quot; And then have it proceed to ruin the campaign for them. Players tend to look for easier way outs when starting and giving them access to powers with so many loopholes isn't going to do them any favors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T22:54:49-08:00","id":16480,"title":"","content":"Plus, the more we can avoid giving those players who like to exploit ambiguous wording excuses to start half-hour arguments with the ST about how a power is intended to work vs. what it technically does or doesn't allow, the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T02:39:49-08:00","id":16537,"title":"","content":"My own houserule regarding Shift Consecuences to use Kittens of Doom against Angels is this: you cannot shift more Damage that what the original can suffer. So a Kitten with only say 4 Health, will only traspass those 4 levels of Damage, not an hypothetic &quot;Dead Condition&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T06:06:18-08:00","id":16590,"title":"","content":"As I like to say - game balance is a hobgoblin. What matters is if the players are stomping on each other's feet; if that is not happening and everyone is having fun then the PC group being combat bad asses means the GM is just going to need to keep that in mind and use other types of challenges as bottle necks. Demon, more so, follows on the heels of the GMC rules paradigm. Combat is no longer entirely special, it's being treated as more or less equal to any other game interaction including rules to speed through it. The Demon powers list treats this as the case, and as a result has some combat powers that match &quot;I win&quot; style powers usually reserved for stealth, talking, healing ... errr everything else. If you want combat to be special like before in a way nWOD has decided it should not be that might mean removing powers that treat it like any other player challenge instead of sacrosanct. But citing that as an issue with Demon as it is, well, that might be missing what GMC did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>J. T. Legal</b><br /> The other kind of rules lawyer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/334-technocratjt","name":"TechnocratJT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar334_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T06:13:42-08:00","id":16597,"title":"","content":"Yeah, maybe the PCs can knock out anyone with a touch, but when they have to deal with Destroyers who begin to corrode their cover, placing metaphorical hooks in every piece of it, and then just have to PULL to have it all fall apart? Knock Out punch isn't gonna help you much then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T06:30:43-08:00","id":16603,"title":"","content":"The issue with game balance though is not that the PCs can become &quot;too good at combat&quot; - that's entirely relative to the challenges the ST sets for them . The issue is that some abilities, by nature of their phenomenal utility, overshadow the abilities of other players who want to participate in that niche but don't have the \u00fcber power. I can't say for sure if Knockout Punch is such a power. Honestly, none of the embeds jumped out as overshadowing to me on my casual read through. But if people are having issues with a power that's just so useful for a particular aspect of play that anyone who doesn't take it can't stand out in that area without the ST specifically setting up situations to make the gimped player feel better about himself... I would say its worth looking into limiting the extent of said power's uses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T06:44:15-08:00","id":16612,"title":"","content":"Out of interest which Embed's do people feel at current are the ones that are &quot;broken&quot; or &quot;overshadowing&quot; in their remit?<br /> <br /> Knock Out Punch has been discusses a lot here.<br /> On the Mend I believe was another, though Matt is editing it now due to its relation to the Break to Mend exploit.<br /> Some people have been mentioning Shift Consequences as well.<br /> <br /> Any others? Also why you think they are problematic? How would you fix this problem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 11-23-2013, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T08:30:31-08:00","id":16651,"title":"","content":"I can't remember what it was called, but the one that creates lucky coincidences seemed like you could use it to do just about anything at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T09:48:38-08:00","id":16674,"title":"","content":"I propose we make a list of all powers that might make a player feel especially effective, stylish or cool and ask them to be removed. It's the only way to be sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>J. T. Legal</b><br /> The other kind of rules lawyer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/334-technocratjt","name":"TechnocratJT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar334_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T10:46:02-08:00","id":16698,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, we can have a bunch of powers that all say &quot;you can do cool stuff, within reason. Your ST is the final arbiter of what counts as within reason.&quot; That's a much better solution than having clearly defined parameters for what powers do or don't allow you to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T11:01:37-08:00","id":16703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TechnocratJT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=16674#post16674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I propose we make a list of all powers that might make a player feel especially effective, stylish or cool and ask them to be removed. It's the only way to be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>All joking aside (well maybe not all). Making a list of Embeds that people feel are so good they may overshadow other options or alter the game dynamic significantly is still a good idea. <br /> <br /> That way Matt can see which ones the player base seems to be taking issue with. Sure, a lot of this might not be that useful to him. However, it was the the community pointing out that On the Mend overshadowed the exploit Break to Heal that made him go back and take a second look. <br /> <br /> If we really are concerned that some of the Embeds as written are really that disruptive then there is no harm in presenting those findings. Matt can either give his take on these things or maybe he'll do some tweaking like with On the Mend. Either way we get good feedback. <br /> <br /> Currently the list is -<br /> <br /> On the Mend (already being addressed)<br /> Knock Out Punch<br /> Shift Consequences <br /> <br /> When listing an Embed it would be good if people could list what they find problematic about the Embed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T11:22:08-08:00","id":16711,"title":"","content":"I honestly think a white room tear down of the power list is wrong headed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>J. T. Legal</b><br /> The other kind of rules lawyer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/334-technocratjt","name":"TechnocratJT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar334_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T12:44:30-08:00","id":16737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TechnocratJT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=16711#post16711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly think a white room tear down of the power list is wrong headed.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair. I'm not asking for White Room power simulations. I'm asking for peoples opinions and hopefully at least some feedback on the different issues that certain Embeds might cause depending on how they are interpreted. <br /> <br /> The aim he is not to objectively &quot;prove&quot; which powers are &quot;broken&quot;. The point is to collect peoples points of view on this stuff in regard to particular examples. <br /> <br /> This could help ST's when they run Demon as it allows for an easy access resource for them to consult when it comes to making sure that they have put the correct caveats that fit the tone of their game on certain potentially problematic Embeds before they start their game.<br /> <br /> Likewise, as I mentioned, the only reason Matt took another look at On the Mend is because someone on these forums point out the fact that it overshadowed an Exploit that did the same thing, which seemed to be against the very themes that Embeds and Exploits are aiming for. So its possible through I continued discussion that we might bring other similar issues to Matt's attention before the PDF is released at the end of the KS. Thereby allowing Matt to get out ahead of the curve with any further Errata that Demon might need to go into its final PDF form. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T15:41:39-08:00","id":16835,"title":"","content":"And if people were:<br /> <br /> 1) Making mechanic specific arguments where another Exploit worked less effectively than an Embed which served the exact same result at all time ( direct heal in the only example case ) that would make sense or, 2) People were playing the game and noting at the table results they felt may have been unintended. That too makes sense.<br /> <br /> Your not asking for either at this point, You want people to simply list powers they think might be too good and complain about that. Your example includes two powers which people have neither played with or really been able to express a concern about past &quot;wow that seems good.&quot; It is pure white room theory about the game. The first response to you was even &quot;there is this power whose name I can't recall which seemed really good.&quot;<br /> <br /> Its a power level complaint request dressed up nice for dinner, but none the less that is what it is until people sit down and play or are able to make a specific argument that an Exploit is doing the exact, and it really was exact, same thing as an Embed but less effectively again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>J. T. Legal</b><br /> The other kind of rules lawyer.","edited":{"userid":334,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/334-technocratjt","user":"TechnocratJT","date":". 11-23-2013, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/334-technocratjt","name":"TechnocratJT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar334_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T16:30:52-08:00","id":16861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TechnocratJT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=16835#post16835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if people were:<br /> <br /> 1) Making mechanic specific arguments where another Exploit worked less effectively than an Embed which served the exact same result at all time ( direct heal in the only example case ) that would make sense or, 2) People were playing the game and noting at the table results they felt may have been unintended. That too makes sense.<br /> <br /> Your not asking for either at this point, You want people to simply list powers they think might be too good and complain about that. Your example includes two powers which people have neither played with or really been able to express a concern about past &quot;wow that seems good.&quot; It is pure white room theory about the game. The first response to you was even &quot;there is this power whose name I can't recall which seemed really good.&quot;<br /> <br /> Its a power level complaint request dressed up nice for dinner, but none the less that is what it is until people sit down and play or are able to make a specific argument that an Exploit is doing the exact, and it really was exact, same thing as an Embed but less effectively again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I was tempted to write a response about the thinly-veiled sarcasm and unnecessarily accusing tone of your post, but I'll just mention it here and then leave it alone. It does not serve the function of the thread. Enough said.<br /> <br /> I've no interest in white-room testing. I'm a big believer its pointless, not to mention I find it utterly boring. What I said in previous post is what I meant. I believe (the foolish optimistic I am on this topic) that people can collate opinions about things and produce a useful resource for other people. <br /> <br /> If people have had a chance to play Demon in the last 11 days since the Kickstarter started then I agree that actual play analysis would be more useful then untested hypothesizing. Which is not to say that untested hypothesizing is completely useless, sometimes you hit the nail on the head without meaning to after all. The point is to just get a debate flowing, collate ideas and such.<br /> <br /> Its not like this all HAS to be regarded by the Dev's or anything. Other ST's and player could come up with interesting points on how to handle certain Embeds that SEEM (actual game testing requires for proof) like they might be a bit tricky. For example, the Knock-Out Punch issue got a lot of replies from other ST's and player that basically mounted up to: <br /> <br /> &quot;Make sure you put caveats on what this power does and does not work on at the games outset, to avoid any later problems during play.&quot; <br /> <br /> I acknowledge that a lot of the Embeds e.g. Shift Consequences, could be solved by applying the same idea to it. However, I've yet to read every single Embed, so I am not sure if the issues people might feel are present with some of them can simply be solved with ST &quot;common sense&quot; (as I'd call it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T16:56:14-08:00","id":16870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=16537#post16537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own houserule regarding Shift Consecuences to use Kittens of Doom against Angels is this: you cannot shift more Damage that what the original can suffer. So a Kitten with only say 4 Health, will only traspass those 4 levels of Damage, not an hypothetic &quot;Dead Condition&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>So then 4 levels in one turn. If not more with multiple demons using that embed to jumpover a combat monster who would take 1 health level if that every other turn. Got it. Totally fine now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T18:12:35-08:00","id":16888,"title":"","content":"If you're fighting an angel, you'd subtract its Resistance if you used Shift Consequences on it (since this would be a meaningful encounter with an NPC that has real consequences for failure). A &quot;combat monster&quot; angel would likely have a <i>massive</i> Resistance (and a massive Power, too). A Combat Monster who's not an Angel would probably have a massive Stamina anyway, and that's what a Shift Consequences attack on a physical being would subtract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T21:54:56-08:00","id":16947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TechnocratJT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=16835#post16835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if people were:<br /> <br /> 1) Making mechanic specific arguments where another Exploit worked less effectively than an Embed which served the exact same result at all time ( direct heal in the only example case ) that would make sense or, 2) People were playing the game and noting at the table results they felt may have been unintended. That too makes sense.<br /> <br /> Your not asking for either at this point, You want people to simply list powers they think might be too good and complain about that. Your example includes two powers which people have neither played with or really been able to express a concern about past &quot;wow that seems good.&quot; It is pure white room theory about the game. The first response to you was even &quot;there is this power whose name I can't recall which seemed really good.&quot;<br /> <br /> Its a power level complaint request dressed up nice for dinner, but none the less that is what it is until people sit down and play or are able to make a specific argument that an Exploit is doing the exact, and it really was exact, same thing as an Embed but less effectively again.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are grossly misrepresenting what it is people are taking issue with. The issue has nothing to do with power level, it is that some powers are not clearly defined in their parameters. Present me with a power that clearly states it does 5 aggravated damage as a reflexive action with no cost to the user and no roll to resist, and I will either find a way to make it work in my games, or ban it. Present me with a power that says you can deal damage of an amount and type that seems appropriate to the situation, and I will complain that it is not sufficiently defined, and will cause problems at the table.<br /> <br /> To use Knockout Punch as an example, since it's been discussed a fair bit in this thread:<br /> <br /> If the intention is for it to work on any and all conscious beings without question, great! Write that in the description and my group and I will decide for ourselves if it is appropriate for our games.<br /> If the intention is for it to work only on beings that can be rendered unconscious, great! Write that in the description and my group and I will decide for ourselves if it is appropriate for our games.<br /> If the intention is for it to work only on people named Steve, great! Write that in the description and my group and I will decide for ourselves if it is appropriate for our games.<br /> If the intention is for me as ST to decide on a whim if it should work or not every time one of my players uses it, I guarantee you there will be a 5-30 minute argument about why I made the wrong call every time I say it doesn't work, probably involving phrases like &quot;prescedent-setting&quot;. As currently written, this is how it reads. As hawthorn and others have pointed out, this can be mitigated by making a blanket ruling like &quot;it only works on corporeal beings and never on angels or other demons&quot; beforehand and making that clear to the group, so we only have to have that argument once rather than every couple of times the power gets used (though with a universal ruling like that, the argument will definitely take longer).<br /> <br /> \u200bPower level is simply not a concern. Unclear or ubiquitously applicable powers are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T22:11:55-08:00","id":16952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=16888#post16888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're fighting an angel, you'd subtract its Resistance if you used Shift Consequences on it (since this would be a meaningful encounter with an NPC that has real consequences for failure). A &quot;combat monster&quot; angel would likely have a <i>massive</i> Resistance (and a massive Power, too). A Combat Monster who's not an Angel would probably have a massive Stamina anyway, and that's what a Shift Consequences attack on a physical being would subtract.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but all you need is one success and all that damage transfers regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T22:13:35-08:00","id":16953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the intention is for me as ST to decide on a whim of it should work or not every time one of my players uses it, I garunteed you we are going to end up having a thirty-minute argument over why I made the wrong ruling every time I say it doesn't work, and that is something I would like to avoid.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I don't have the luxury of being able to tell my close personal friends with a few annoying rules-based gaming habits 'stfu and sit down' or 'don't play at my table' if I want to have a table at all. I know I'm far from the only person in this situation. I'd also really like a clearer guide for what's reasonable because I am <i>not</i> a game designer. Perceiving 'well, this seems out of whack' doesn't give me any special insight into into fixing it, and I'd expect the people who wrote the cool and minimally problematic remaining 95%+ of the system to have a clear picture of intended use cases.<br /> <br /> The White Room has only been brought up by people attacking the desire for rule clarity. In contrast to Break to Mend/On the Mend - in which I can imagine no situation where the as-written Exploit is more useful or less risky than the as-written Embed - the issues in Knockout Blow and Shift Consequence proceed from bringing in factors outside the apparently intended use cases. I'd really like to keep a quick, nonlethal takedown power as it's incredibly genre-appropriate. I'd prefer it not to be something that sneers down from on high at every combat ability that deals in mere dots of damage, which does not strike me as its intended use but I can forsee getting into arguments over.<br /> <br /> Shift Consequence... just plain needs more clarity. Does it transfer a condition like 'dead' even if the original target was, well, a kitten (which seems silly on its face to me, but...)? If what it's actually transferring is, say, 'the bullet hit the angel Machariel rather than this poor kitten' should the attack be rerolled as if the new target was the original? If nWoD actually had a two-stage hit-damage mechanic that'd be real easy to implement, but it doesn't, and I don't know where to stick the split...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:56:11-08:00","id":17001,"title":"","content":"&quot;Dead&quot; is not a Condition. Capital &quot;C&quot;. We have a list of them. I'm not sure where a factor outside the use cases has been brought up, rather I have seen people argue it transfers damage too easily. That's is not a clarity issue, nor does it seem outside a use case. The idea this is some established use case being unclear has suddenly come up in response to my pointing out people have not played with the power. Which almost always, short a seriously good roll, causes a cover check. Arguing that's not white room is thinking white room means a fight off as opposed to it being any analysis of power out of context. People need to play with a power like that not theorize its bad.<br /> <br /> I give that Knockout punch does not say it can't effect things unable to being knocked out in that fashion. But again that was not really the complaint being made. Laughs off other attacks is not &quot;used outside of intended case.&quot; Its &quot;this is very effective and I think that's unfair,&quot; and &quot;players might ask to use this ability on things that can't actually be effected by the result because the result never happens to them&quot; does not strike me as some complex use case that each power needs carefully cataloged.<br /> <br /> But you are all correct. I am being very grouchy. I apologize for the tone before, I think the direction and intent of this thread is very wrong headed, but it was not a reason to be rude. But honestly I think this threads goal is the type game designers run away from, and it does depend on worries that have not arisen in actual use or in comparison to context or totality of the rules and other powers. Which is a good way to make anyone whose job it is to write those rules write this exercise off, and allow people to instead engage in that favorite pastime - explaining how something is a problem without evidence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>J. T. Legal</b><br /> The other kind of rules lawyer.","edited":{"userid":334,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/334-technocratjt","user":"TechnocratJT","date":". 11-24-2013, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/334-technocratjt","name":"TechnocratJT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar334_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:31:13-08:00","id":17025,"title":"","content":"I appreciate it, and apologize for getting a bit snippy myself. Personally, I don't see the problem in expressing concerns about potential abuses of high-utility powers to the designers. We're not demanding things be changed or we won't buy the game. We're just offering our perspectives on things we see potential problems with based on prior experience with similarly broad use powers, and hoping our opinions are taken into consideration. That, and I really enjoy debating game design philosophy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> On a personal note, I find you guys here on the WoD forums infinitely more agreeable than the folks on the D&amp;D forums I used to frequent. The generally constructive attitude is very refreshing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T03:39:04-08:00","id":17064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=16870#post16870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So then 4 levels in one turn. If not more with multiple demons using that embed to jumpover a combat monster who would take 1 health level if that every other turn. Got it. Totally fine now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a rule of thumb. I believe the emotional investment is also to be taken into account to determine wich effects can be transfered and from wich target to another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T04:24:22-08:00","id":17070,"title":"","content":"Given the way combat works after the GMC revision I'm not too concerned with knockout punch. If a player's intent is to not deal with a threat right now then it's plenty useful, but the second they are interested in using combat to effect longer lasting meaningful narrative changes that goes out the window. A player using Knockout Punch is giving up the chance to Beat Down their enemy. They do no long lasting damage, do not force willpower expenditures, and still need to beat their defense with a stacking penalty for failure which against any capable combat character is no guarantee, especially if they are built to be a melee combatant (which means prioritizing strength) unless they are willing to expend willpower to do it.<br /> <br /> Consistent use of Knockout Punch is a good way to avoid conflict for a time, but under the GMC rules its also a good way to not fulfill aspirations, avoid risking cover, not take any damage at all, , etc. If you don't take any risks the GMC rules you'll find yourself gaining very little in the way of beats and not really resolving situations.<br /> <br /> I haven't seen it in play, but I don't really see it proving to be too heavy handed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/737-campbell","name":"Campbell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T10:03:21-08:00","id":17160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Campbell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=17070#post17070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the way combat works after the GMC revision I'm not too concerned with knockout punch. If a player's intent is to not deal with a threat right now then it's plenty useful, but the second they are interested in using combat to effect longer lasting meaningful narrative changes that goes out the window. A player using Knockout Punch is giving up the chance to Beat Down their enemy. They do no long lasting damage, do not force willpower expenditures, and still need to beat their defense with a stacking penalty for failure which against any capable combat character is no guarantee, especially if they are built to be a melee combatant (which means prioritizing strength) unless they are willing to expend willpower to do it. Consistent use of Knockout Punch is a good way to avoid conflict for a time, but under the GMC rules its also a good way to not fulfill aspirations, avoid risking cover, not take any damage at all, , etc. If you don't take any risks the GMC rules you'll find yourself gaining very little in the way of beats and not really resolving situations. I haven't seen it in play, but I don't really see it proving to be too heavy handed.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree this is the intent , but in practice it allows you to bypass the combat system entirely and take a target out of the fight in one attack, regardless of their health and healing abilities. That said, maybe a good solution would be to follow the example if merciless gunman. Now there is a very, very strong power that doesn't strike me as problematic because it only serves to expedite fights that are meant to be quick and cinematic anyway, and still helps in the big important fights within the combat system. Why not have knockout punch work as written for combats that the ST agrees can be down and dirty, and then have a slightly different but still useful function for &quot;real&quot; combat that doesn't bypass the whole fight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T11:58:35-08:00","id":17202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=17064#post17064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a rule of thumb. I believe the emotional investment is also to be taken into account to determine wich effects can be transfered and from wich target to another.</div> </div> </div> </div>\uff29\u2019m sorry but if the power needs you determine whether it works under every situation without clear rules so that regardless of the capability of the ST you have to houserule it in some way. Then the power has issues. You shouldn't have to houserule a power to make clear and focused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T12:37:12-08:00","id":17227,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't care for the &quot;it's not broken because I can fix it&quot; school of thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T13:12:50-08:00","id":17263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Campbell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=17070#post17070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the way combat works after the GMC revision I'm not too concerned with knockout punch. If a player's intent is to not deal with a threat right now then it's plenty useful, but the second they are interested in using combat to effect longer lasting meaningful narrative changes that goes out the window. A player using Knockout Punch is giving up the chance to Beat Down their enemy. They do no long lasting damage, do not force willpower expenditures, and still need to beat their defense with a stacking penalty for failure which against any capable combat character is no guarantee, especially if they are built to be a melee combatant (which means prioritizing strength) unless they are willing to expend willpower to do it.<br /> <br /> Consistent use of Knockout Punch is a good way to avoid conflict for a time, but under the GMC rules its also a good way to not fulfill aspirations, avoid risking cover, not take any damage at all, , etc. If you don't take any risks the GMC rules you'll find yourself gaining very little in the way of beats and not really resolving situations.<br /> <br /> I haven't seen it in play, but I don't really see it proving to be too heavy handed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a vastly more constructive response than the others, particularly the reminder that Strength drives normal melee attacks in nWoD (too much Shadowrun here).<br /> I'm not entirely on board with the idea that succeeding too easily is a player drawback so much as a force limiting the possible narrative for the entire table, but eh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T13:44:32-08:00","id":17280,"title":"","content":"I don't care for &quot;It's Not Broken If I Can Fix It&quot; either. There is a difference between &quot;This Must Be Adjusted For Your Group's Preferences&quot; and general lack of clarity. I would really rather it be gotten right out of the starting gate. We have lots of time right now to make corrections, so now we be a good idea to deal with any issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T02:05:24-08:00","id":19051,"title":"","content":"Wow I just read Raw Materials and that is insane! This need more limits, whats stopping someone from breaking a Trashcan to get a Trashcan's worth of solid gold, or hell a Diamond the size of a trashcan! Or breaking a bookshelf to get a bunch of books on the secret blueprints of a building. Or breaking a car to get some Plutonium... ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T07:58:23-08:00","id":19182,"title":"","content":"I thought Raw Materials applied to objects of roughly similar size and value? Either that or my brain just slipped it in while I was reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 11-27-2013, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T08:30:37-08:00","id":19193,"title":"","content":"Same Size, but it seems that what you get in exchange also has to exist somewhere, is not a creation power proper. So the answer is probably that if there are not such thing as a trashcan-sized diamond, then you are not geting one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T09:14:01-08:00","id":19211,"title":"","content":"And if one exists but is still buried deep in the earth, you might be waiting a Very Long Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T12:51:27-08:00","id":19315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=19193#post19193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same Size, but it seems that what you get in exchange also has to exist somewhere, is not a creation power proper. So the answer is probably that if there are not such thing as a trashcan-sized diamond, then you are not geting one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The more practical use is a trashcan into +5 sniper rifle or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T15:08:26-08:00","id":19372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=16861#post16861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've no interest in white-room testing. I'm a big believer its pointless, not to mention I find it utterly boring. What I said in previous post is what I meant. I believe (the foolish optimistic I am on this topic) that people can collate opinions about things and produce a useful resource for other people.<br /> <br /> If people have had a chance to play Demon in the last 11 days since the Kickstarter started then I agree that actual play analysis would be more useful then untested hypothesizing. Which is not to say that untested hypothesizing is completely useless, sometimes you hit the nail on the head without meaning to after all. The point is to just get a debate flowing, collate ideas and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>For whatever this may be worth...<br /> <br /> While I've not gotten to play or run Demon in the past 11 days (or play it ever), I did run one of the playtest groups. One of the PC's in that group had as his Embeds Strike First, Knockout Punch, Hush, and In My Pocket.<br /> <br /> He used Knockout Punch....twice, I think. Once to knock out a guy who'd mugged another member of the Ring, and once on a cop in a bathroom (don't ask). In the latter case, I was actually quite lenient and let him chain it together with Hush and Strike First. Poor guy was just standing there at the urinal, doing his thing, and as soon as he finished, boom. There it went. At no point was Knockout Punch an actual issue (although I think I did make Defense apply, and it looks like that's in the rules now - don't remember for sure what was in the playtest material). The story moved along just fine, and nothing was &quot;broken,&quot; thrown off the rails, or what-have-you. None of the other players felt overshadowed by what that one character was doing. Incidentally, when the Ring later got into a big combat, that character didn't end up doing much, actually - the Guardian ended up doing the most damage due to having Blade Hand as a Demonic form ability.<br /> <br /> That's the only actual play experience I have with the Embed, so take that for what it's worth. I do agree that seeing how something works in play is much more suitable and satisfying than any &quot;white room&quot; scenario.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T15:29:40-08:00","id":19385,"title":"","content":"A couple things about Knockout Punch as currently presented that I feel are being skimmed over:<br /> 1) It's cumulatively penalized per miss in a scene on top of the resistance by Defense \u2014 which, lest we forget, is higher in GMC's rules than it was in the old nWoD system.<br /> 2) Even a cursory attempt to revive the victim works unless you rolled an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> Its utility is drastically undercut in scenarios where you have to deal with any degree of numbers disadvantage that allows one enemy to take a moment to wake their fallen comrade. Meanwhile it's still very much useful as a power for quickly dispatching a lone guard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-27-2013, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T16:38:00-08:00","id":19424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=19385#post19385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple things about Knockout Punch as currently presented that I feel are being skimmed over:<br /> 1) It's cumulatively penalized per extra use in a scene on top of the resistance by Defense \u2014 which, lest we forget, is higher in GMC's rules than it was in the old nWoD system.<br /> 2) Even a cursory attempt to revive the victim works unless you rolled an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> Its utility is drastically undercut in scenarios where you have to deal with any degree of numbers disadvantage that allows one enemy to take a moment to wake their fallen comrade. Meanwhile it's still very <b>much useful as a power for quickly dispatching a lone guard.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Bolded for emphasis. <br /> <br /> Absolutely - which, considering this is a game about techgnostic espionage, means that the power is thematically appropriate, I feel. I would certainly allow it to be used with things other than punches, as well - a grab and slam into a nearby hard surface or a choke hold, for instance - because they fit the genre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T23:15:33-08:00","id":19576,"title":"","content":"I was just reading over the &quot;On the Mend&quot; embed and realized as a Demon's Primum increases he becomes able to reliably heal agg damage far easier than lethal. For example, a Demon with Primum 4 heals 4 agg with one success, while he would only heal 1 lethal with that same roll. Perhaps for internal balance healing lethal should become successes rolled or Primum rating, whichever is higher. I'd also then swap healing agg to successes rolled or Primum, whichever is lower. That at least feels closer to keeping with agg damage being harder to heal than lethal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I'm immortal, I've been right so far&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/301-bwchism","name":"bwchism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T04:45:31-08:00","id":19657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=19385#post19385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple things about Knockout Punch as currently presented that I feel are being skimmed over:<br /> 1) It's cumulatively penalized per miss in a scene on top of the resistance by Defense \u2014 which, lest we forget, is higher in GMC's rules than it was in the old nWoD system.<br /> 2) Even a cursory attempt to revive the victim works unless you rolled an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> Its utility is drastically undercut in scenarios where you have to deal with any degree of numbers disadvantage that allows one enemy to take a moment to wake their fallen comrade. Meanwhile it's still very much useful as a power for quickly dispatching a lone guard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you plan on barraging your players with multiple angels they have no hope of winning again, the rules don't explicitly disallow you from knocking out an angel with it. Even if there were multiple opponents one would still need to waste his turn to revive him making it much better to just knock someone out making the fight easier in general as the character would have to reroll initiative to get back into the fight afterward.<br /> <br /> An ST shouldn't have to look at this power and gauges whether it works or doesn't work every time though. My problem has nothing to do with the power of the embeds but rather how vague broad they are to the point where an experienced ST will easily understand how to houserule the power and an inexperienced st will see his campaign ruined because one of his players decided that sever powers when used in conjunction can win any game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T06:09:29-08:00","id":19683,"title":"","content":"This may be a method of resolution that is too simple but in my mind, as a potential player with admitted leanings toward wanting more awesome than not---I might ask if it were possible to use Knockout Punch on an angel who hasn't revealed its splendor (gone loud) so long as I got the jump on it. Basically, if it were obeying what it is to be human. Hypothetical: Angel Bob has been given an order to deal with any demons by the GM in as subtle a fashion as possible. Demon Jim has no compunction about taking down Angel Bob by whatever means. Angel Bob doesn't adapt quick enough to the mission at hand and Demon Jim knocks him out. Now---do I expect to be able to kill Angel Bob in his knocked out state? No. I mean, I could try but Angel Bob is only human to the eye. A gunshot or a knife wound can possibly do in a Demon but an Angel is still jacked to the GM. Doesn't that confer unto it inherent fortitude that would make an attack after this knockout unwise to say the least? &quot;Best&quot; case scenario I would envision being possible is I get the drop on an angel while he's cavorting in the meat suit, balance the desire to kill him with some other Embed/Exploit against the inevitable shitstorm that will follow and hope for the best if I follow through. But I can't imagine there will be any Storyteller that would let me continue to fortuitously knock, drop, and kill an Angel followed by an unimpeded escape with no ramifications. All that said, there's still the fuzzy issue of &quot;Can this work on an angel in any circumstance, I.e. knocking him out while 'human'&quot;. There may be value in clarifying (if it isn't already---I probably should have read through the whole thing a couple times before opining) an angel's relative vulnerabilities when moving about as a human. I've seen inferences made based on how an angel doesn't need sleep should indicate its ability or lack thereof to lose consciousness. But that wouldn't fly for me necessarily. Just because it doesn't require rest doesn't mean it can't be imposed upon to lose awareness of being via an uppercut. Those are different things. Sorry for the imprecision but I hope the input of a neophyte in general to all these systems has offered something of value to the discussion. Reading through these posts helps me a little even though it's still heavily abstracted to eventually (I hope) know how to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":257,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","user":"Calrabjohns","date":".  It didn't paragraph like I meant it to. Hope this does the trick. 11-28-2013, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","name":"Calrabjohns","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T06:17:20-08:00","id":19687,"title":"","content":"I don't know why it won't break properly. I am posting on my phone. If someone knows how I can fix that glob of text, I would be grateful. Until then, I'll leave it there (it took a little time to finish) but with the understanding that no-one will read it given how it looks. Apologies for the Akira blob of text at the moment though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","name":"Calrabjohns","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T06:30:30-08:00","id":19691,"title":"","content":"If I'm using real combat rules then the fight is <i>already</i> considered important and a one hit incapaciation is probably not particularly good narratively.<br /> <br /> Dispatching the lone guard on the door? Down and Dirty. Taking out the mafioso's goons in his office while you threaten him? Down and Dirty.<br /> <br /> Being confronted by the Mage whose ritual preparations you've destroyed becaue you thought it was an arcane matrix under construction? Yeah, that's not having a KO Punch end it in one, so it seems I'll just change it...maybe make it cause the Stunned Tilt...treat it like an attack that treats it's weapon bonus as 2 or 3 for the purposes of causing the Stunned Tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T18:23:10-08:00","id":21378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=13965#post13965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and I don't think I'd let Knockout Punch work on an angel. But it would depend on the angel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarification on this point would be appreciated within the rules. I don't mind running my games on a common law system but it seems like there's a specific intent behind putting a power like &quot;knockout punch&quot; in the game and I'd appreciate a rules system that makes the rationale behind that decision clearer.<br /> <br /> In game I'm obviously going to have to decide what is and isn't appropriate, and it would be nice to know how the power was intended to be used and what obstacles it was intended to trivialise and what obstacles it wasn't.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>-<br /> Formerly Inquisitive Englishman","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/930-inqy","name":"Inqy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T20:55:29-08:00","id":21436,"title":"","content":"After reading through bits of the thread, my take away is that there should be a few more boxes in the text telling us &quot;If any of these powers are causing issues then change them, perhaps by adding resistance traits. Make sure you discuss things with the players when the rules change though.&quot; That, at least, will clearly communicate the ethos of the designer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T01:00:03-08:00","id":21484,"title":"","content":"One of my players wants to use Momentum to borrow successes from an enemy's attack, and then put them into Just Bruised, making him damn hard to kill. Am I right in thinking this is wrong because they're both Reflexive Actions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T01:38:25-08:00","id":21491,"title":"","content":"I didn;t think there was a limit to the number of Relfexive actions you could take in a turn.<br /> <br /> Sounds to me like one of those Tai-Chi/Aikido style things where you take your opponent's power and use it against them so I don't think I'd have an issue with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T03:08:16-08:00","id":21518,"title":"","content":"If we go by the corebook? Breathing, walking, seeing... All those are reflexive. You don't take a moment to do each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T06:15:31-08:00","id":21584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=21484#post21484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my players wants to use Momentum to borrow successes from an enemy's attack, and then put them into Just Bruised, making him damn hard to kill. Am I right in thinking this is wrong because they're both Reflexive Actions?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually really clever. You're right that, because they're both reflexive actions, that makes the character continually badass, but as I think I've demonstrated, I'm generally in favor of badass characters. The real question is, could you then take an attack as your action after that? Yeah, I think so. If the Storyteller feels like the character is overusing it, there's always the probability-hunting angels to fall back on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T06:57:13-08:00","id":21596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=21584#post21584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually really clever. You're right that, because they're both reflexive actions, that makes the character continually badass, but as I think I've demonstrated, I'm generally in favor of badass characters. The real question is, could you then take an attack as your action after that? Yeah, I think so. If the Storyteller feels like the character is overusing it, there's always the probability-hunting angels to fall back on.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably just an extreme difference in ideology but should an St punish a Player for using his powers with perfectly valid tactics? I mean if the intention is that you can use all these powers at once he's not doing anything wrong per rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T07:06:16-08:00","id":21599,"title":"","content":"What happens when the Hunter Angels bounce off through some clever combination of Embeds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T07:06:42-08:00","id":21600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=21596#post21596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is probably just an extreme difference in ideology but should an St punish a Player for using his powers with perfectly valid tactics? I mean if the intention is that you can use all these powers at once he's not doing anything wrong per rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules have a context within the story, though. So it isn't necessarily &quot;punishing&quot; a player for using valid tactics so much as it's fitting everything within the narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T07:16:11-08:00","id":21602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=21600#post21600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The rules have a context within the story, though. So it isn't necessarily &quot;punishing&quot; a player for using valid tactics so much as it's fitting everything within the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have to send angels for using powers that don't cost aether aren't Blatant reality shenanigans like exploits and preventing something which you already allowed in the first place then yes. It's punishing a player for using valid tactics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T07:52:56-08:00","id":21624,"title":"","content":"Perhaps stick a generic rule at the top of the Embeds section that cals out clearly that repeated use of any Embed within a scene attracts God-machine attention and causes Compromise eventually?<br /> <br /> Maybe make it cumulative across all Demons in the scene too. So we don't have the two non-combatants using Just Bruised+Momentum constantly as their contribution to the fight scene.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, exceptional success on Just Bruised = 0 damage. Someone with a good dice pool (4+3 isn't unrealistic for a normal character) + Momentum vs. a powerful Angel (say rolling &gt;20 dice like a rank 4 or 5) could not unrealistically expect to be rolling 15 dice...which averages an Exceptional Success. Not bad, defence that gets better the tougher the opponent <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Left or Right vs. Ambush vs. Diversion (can any of the playtesters say how they found using these alongside each other?)<br /> <br /> Download Knowledge vs. Fungible Knowledge vs. Borrowed Expertise (At first glance Download seems better)<br /> <br /> Ambush vs. Strike First (Ambush seems better as it helps everyone)<br /> <br /> Turn Blade vs. Just Bruised (Just Bruised seems to work on everything thus making it more universaally applicable)<br /> <br /> These seem to share a fair bit of overlap and I'd be worried their small nuances in use may make one of them the obvious pick and other...really specialised only or not taken at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T08:54:02-08:00","id":21666,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> <br /> Calling in the Angels as a response to repeated use, can't you use Interference to diffuse the immediate threat?<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Just Bruised + Partial Manifestation of Demonic Form Wound Healing + Interference = Near unhurtable.<br /> <br /> Add in Momentum and On the Mend and you're pretty damned good at tanking hits...to the point where armour is probably irrelevant to you.<br /> <br /> Just need to find a way to resist mental influence and your Demon super tank could well be ready <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 12-02-2013, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:17:01-08:00","id":21687,"title":"","content":"If the Demon becomes a prominent nuisance for the God Machine? It's gonna tailor specific angels to deal with him. If you continuously blind it's operatives with Magnesium Flare, the angels hunting you will come packing Blind Sense. It's just how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T19:38:31-08:00","id":23457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=21666#post21666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.<br /> <br /> Calling in the Angels as a response to repeated use, can't you use Interference to diffuse the immediate threat?</div> </div> </div> </div>A single-digit penalty to looking for you is only going to hold them off for so long before they start breaking out the high-Rank hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-04-2013, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T21:55:14-08:00","id":23530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=21596#post21596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is probably just an extreme difference in ideology but should an St punish a Player for using his powers with perfectly valid tactics? I mean if the intention is that you can use all these powers at once he's not doing anything wrong per rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally I would agree it sounds like punishing the player. In this specific context though sending angels after players for regularly using the same trick makes perfect sense. The character is setting a pattern, and the God-Machine is really good at picking up patterns. It's not obvious like some other things, but over time it's definitely the kind of thing that would be noticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T22:44:04-08:00","id":23548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=23530#post23530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normally I would agree it sounds like punishing the player. In this specific context though sending angels after players for regularly using the same trick makes perfect sense. The character is setting a pattern, and the God-Machine is really good at picking up patterns. It's not obvious like some other things, but over time it's definitely the kind of thing that would be noticed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, if the G-M can take advantage of demons expecting it to stick to tetrapartite structures, it'd be kind of silly to expect it not to be able to work to counter use of Embeds \u2014 i.e. the powers that use loopholes in reality <i>that it made.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-05-2013, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T04:52:00-08:00","id":23676,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised no one (I've seen) has any problem with the splat-stripping numina Resurrection. Not an embed, but now you can lose your awakening or lycanthropy. And it's not even limited to angels,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T06:12:00-08:00","id":23707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=23548#post23548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, if the G-M can take advantage of demons expecting it to stick to tetrapartite structures, it'd be kind of silly to expect it not to be able to work to counter use of Embeds \u2014 i.e. the powers that use loopholes in reality <i>that it made.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Right, exactly. <br /> <br /> Now, <i>with that said</i> I agree that generally, I don't like punishing players for valid tactics. But see, you can't expect to use the same trick every time and expect your enemies not to pick up on the patterns. If the player wants kudos for being clever, I'm all about that. I'll give Beats for clever tactics, I'll let the players have awesome victories with clever tactics...but you'd better keep coming up with new material, because you'd bet your ass the God-Machine will adapt. <br /> <br /> As for Resurrection, you do understand it only works on people who have <i>died</i>, right? You can't just use it on a live werewolf and turn him into a wolf-blooded. You have to kill him first, at which point the splat-stripping bit of the Numen isn't really the relevant point anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T09:52:42-08:00","id":30468,"title":"","content":"I don't want to make a new thread (and the title is a bit fitting). I've got a few &quot;problems&quot; or more questinos in regards to alibi.<br /> -What happens when a vampire tries to turn the alibi into another vampire?<br /> -The alibi does it have the covers memories / knowledge or the demons? (example: Rushed soulpact and the demon doesnt know anything at all about the cover and what it regularly does)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T10:20:14-08:00","id":30474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds?p=30468#post30468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to make a new thread (and the title is a bit fitting). I've got a few &quot;problems&quot; or more questinos in regards to alibi. -What happens when a vampire tries to turn the alibi into another vampire? -The alibi does it have the covers memories / knowledge or the demons? (example: Rushed soulpact and the demon doesnt know anything at all about the cover and what it regularly does)</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't recall what alibi does, so I can't answer that. But I do know covers have the Demon's memories and not the memories of the person they were. So obviously rushed pacts should only be a last resort - if you're just about to blow a cover and need a new one right away. As long as it lasts long enough to lay the ground work for a more solid cover, it'll do. But if you know nothing about the person, a rushed cover will get compromised very quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}